With -fopenmp and --offload-arch=, the driver runs Flang's offload jobs for
each source: the host's bitcode, with offload entries for the GPUs; each
GPU's bitcode, matching them; one offload binary of the GPUs' code; and the
host's object file from its bitcode, with the binary embedded. The link is
Clang's with -fopenmp and --offload-arch=, which runs the linker wrapper.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-registered-target

RUN: merkc -### -fopenmp --offload-arch=gfx1030 -O2 -L/omp/lib %S/Inputs/sumsq.m -o prog 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s
CHECK:      "-fc1" "-emit-llvm-bc" "-fopenmp" "-O2" "--offload-targets=amdgpu-amd-amdhsa" "-o" "[[HOST:[^"]*sumsq-[^"]*\.bc]]" "{{[^"]*}}sumsq.m"{{$}}
CHECK-NEXT: "-fc1" "-emit-llvm-bc" "-fopenmp" "-triple" "amdgpu10.30-amd-amdhsa" "-O2" "-fopenmp-is-target-device" "-fopenmp-host-ir-file-path" "[[HOST]]" "-o" "[[DEVICE:[^"]*sumsq-gfx1030-[^"]*\.bc]]" "{{[^"]*}}sumsq.m"{{$}}
CHECK-NEXT: "{{[^"]*}}llvm-offload-binary{{(\.exe)?}}" "-o" "[[BINARY:[^"]*\.out]]" "--image=file=[[DEVICE]],triple=amdgpu10.30-amd-amdhsa,arch=gfx1030,kind=openmp"{{$}}
CHECK-NEXT: "-fc1" "-emit-obj" "-fopenmp" "-O2" "-fembed-offload-object=[[BINARY]]" "--offload-targets=amdgpu-amd-amdhsa" "-o" "[[OBJECT:[^"]*sumsq-[^"]*\.o]]" "-x" "ir" "[[HOST]]"{{$}}
CHECK-NEXT: "{{[^"]*}}clang{{(\.exe)?}}" "-fopenmp" "--offload-arch=gfx1030" "-o" "prog" "[[OBJECT]]" "-L/omp/lib" "-L{{[^"]*}}lib" "-lmerkstd" "-lmerkrt" "-lm"{{$}}

With -v, Clang shows the link's own jobs too, such as the linker wrapper's.
RUN: merkc -### -v -fopenmp --offload-arch=gfx1030 %S/Inputs/sumsq.m -o prog 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VERBOSE
VERBOSE: "{{[^"]*}}clang{{(\.exe)?}}" "-v" "-fopenmp" "--offload-arch=gfx1030" "-o" "prog"

Two GPUs give a device job each, and two images in the binary.
RUN: merkc -### -fopenmp --offload-arch=gfx1030,gfx90a -c %S/Inputs/sumsq.m 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TWO
TWO:      "-triple" "amdgpu10.30-amd-amdhsa"
TWO:      "-triple" "amdgpu9.0a-amd-amdhsa"
TWO:      "--image=file={{[^"]*}}-gfx1030-{{[^"]*}},triple=amdgpu10.30-amd-amdhsa,arch=gfx1030,kind=openmp" "--image=file={{[^"]*}}-gfx90a-{{[^"]*}},triple=amdgpu9.0a-amd-amdhsa,arch=gfx90a,kind=openmp"{{$}}
TWO:      "-fc1" "-emit-obj" {{.*}} "-o" "sumsq.o" "-x" "ir"
TWO-NOT:  clang

-E has no offload jobs.
RUN: merkc -### -fopenmp --offload-arch=gfx1030 -E %S/Inputs/sumsq.m 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PRE
PRE: "-fc1" "-E" "-fopenmp" "{{[^"]*}}sumsq.m"{{$}}

RUN: not merkc -### --offload-arch=gfx1030 %S/Inputs/sumsq.m 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NO-OMP
NO-OMP: merkc: error: --offload-arch needs -fopenmp
RUN: not merkc -### -fopenmp --offload-arch=sm_80 %S/Inputs/sumsq.m 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NVPTX
NVPTX: merkc: error: offloading to 'sm_80' is not supported yet: only AMD GPUs, such as gfx1030, are
RUN: not merkc -### -fopenmp --offload-arch=gfx1030 -S %S/Inputs/sumsq.m 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ASM
ASM: merkc: error: -S with --offload-arch is not supported yet
